# Netlify redirect rules. Vite copies everything in public/ into dist/, so this
# file ships inside the published folder and therefore works for BOTH a
# Git-connected build and a drag-and-drop deploy of dist/ (which never sees the
# netlify.toml at the repo root).
#
# First matching rule wins, so the specific rule comes before the catch-all.

# The .htaccess beside it is Apache configuration for InfinityFree. Netlify
# does not interpret it and would otherwise serve it as a plain text file.
/.htaccess      /index.html   404

# SPA routing: any path that is not a real file is handed to the app.
# Status 200 rewrites instead of redirecting, so the router still sees the
# original URL — /study/courses stays /study/courses in the address bar.
/*              /index.html   200
